 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 510 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law relating\nto the imposition of a hotel and motel tax in the town of Woodbury, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5191",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5191-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 510 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5191\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 510 of the laws of 2016,\namending the tax law relating to the imposition of a hotel and motel tax\nin the town of Woodbury, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation extends for an additional three years the authorization\nof the Town of Woodbury in Orange County, to impose by local law, a tax\non hotel and motel occupancy of up to five percent of the charge.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSections 1: Extends the effectiveness of the current authorization for\nan additional 3 years.\n\nSection 2: Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2016, the Legislature authorized the Town of Woodbury to impose a\nhotel and motel tax at a rate not to exceed 5% of the per diem rental\nrate for each room. The existing authorization for the tax expires at\nthe end of 2019 and the Town has asked for a 3-year extension based on\nthe positive impact the receipts from the tax have had on the town\ngovernment's attempts to keep local property taxes under the state tax\ncap.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state. The town will collect additional revenues which will\nbe used to reduce the burden on local taxpayers.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
